{
  "raw": {
    "https://canisiusuniversity-puzzlehr.icims.com/jobs/12350/facilities-operations-coordinator/job": {
      "title": "Facilities Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Facilities Operations Coordinator Location : Location US-NY-Buffalo Category Education Position Type Full-Time Position Overview Now Hiring! Facilities Operations Coordinator 📍 Location: Facilities Management 🕒 Schedule: M-F, 8:30am-4:30pm 💰 Pay: $25.65 per hour 📄 Position Type: Full-Time Why Join Canisius University Canisius University serves approximately 2,500 undergraduate and graduate students. As a Catholic and Jesuit University, Canisius has its foundation in the fundamental values of academic excellence, leadership, faith and social justice. Canisius is committed to educating and preparing men and women to become leaders in their professions and their communities, and in service to humanity. The University is an equal opportunity employer committed to recruiting, supporting, and fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff, and students. What We Offer: ✅ Salary: $25.65 per hour* ✅ Comprehensive Insurance Benefits – Health, Dental, Vision, Life and Long-Term Disability available the first of the month after the employee’s date of hire ✅ 403(b) with Company Contribution – Plan for your future with confidence – contribution from the university is available after one year of employment ✅ Paid Time Off – Includes vacation time, personal time, sick time, and paid holidays ✅ Tuition Benefits – Available for full-time employees and their qualified dependents *Please note that the compensation information is a good faith estimate of the base pay for this position. The selected candidate’s compensation package for this position will be provided during the interview process. Your Role as Facilities Operations Coordinator: Canisius University seeks an experienced and organized Facilities Operations Coordinator to oversee day-to-day physical plant operations, master budget administration, and external vendor partnerships across campus. Rooted in our Jesuit values of service and community stewardship, this role ensures university facilities operate smoothly, efficiently, and within financial targets. The ideal candidate will combine strong fiscal responsibility—managing both operating and capital development budgets—with active project oversight and robust vendor management. Key Responsibilities: Budget Management & Financial Monitoring Direct the formulation, review, and execution of the Facilities Management annual operating budget. Participate in the multi-year Capital planning process, collaborating with campus leaders to identify, estimate, and prioritize capital improvement projects. Monitor monthly expenditures against operational and capital budgets, perform variance analyses, and produce financial reports for university leadership. Process purchase orders, approve service invoices, track change orders, and maintain accurate ledger documentation for all facility-related accounts. Forecast long-term renewal needs and maintain reserve planning models for major infrastructure assets (HVAC, roofs, paving, building envelopes). Vendor Relations & Contract Management Serve as the primary university liaison for third-party facility service providers, including HVAC technicians, electrical contractors, custodial teams, security systems, and waste management. Participate in Request for Proposals (RFPs), build scopes of work (SOWs), and lead bidding in alignment with university procurement guidelines. Establish key performance indicators (KPIs) to audit vendor work quality, ensure Service Level Agreement (SLA) compliance, and resolve contract disputes promptly. Onboard new contractors, ensuring compliance with institutional safety policies, campus access protocols, and insurance/licensing requirements. Operational Coordination & Campus Support Coordinate and monitor routine preventative maintenance schedules, facility work orders, and emergency repairs across campus academic, residential, and administrative buildings. Collaborate with Event Services, Athletics, and Student Affairs to provide operational support for campus events, setups, and seasonal transitions. Maintain facility management software (CMMS) to track work orders, inventory, and lifecycle logs. Perform and manage department accounts payable and receivable functions, including the preparation of I-Documents, Procard, and purchase orders. Implement, interpret, and review bargaining unit employees’ contracts. Organize and file office documents and records Oversee work-study and summer grounds students hiring process. Assist in campus sustainability initiatives, energy management tracking, and compliance with local, state, and environmental safety regulations. Perform tasks, duties, and special projects assigned. What You Need to Succeed: ✔ Qualifications: KNOWLEDGE, Skills & Abilities: Technical Skills: Proficiency with Work Order/CMMS systems, ERP finance modules (e.g., Ellucian Banner, Workday), and advanced Microsoft Excel skills (pivot tables, modeling, forecasting). Computer proficiency with Microsoft Word, Excel, and the ability to learn additional programs. Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and external contractors. Ability to work occasionally during off-hours, including weekends. Commitment to the Jesuit mission and tradition of Canisius University. Eligible to work in the United States. Education & CERTIFICATIONS : Bachelor’s degree in Facilities Management, Business Management, Construction Management, Finance, or a related field (or equivalent combination of education and direct professional experience). Experience: 2 or more years of progressive experience in facilities operations, physical plant management, or capital project coordination. Fiscal Insight: Proven experience building operating budgets, managing multi-year capital projects, and performing financial forecasting and ledger reconciliations. Vendor Operations: Background drafting RFPs, negotiating contracts, and holding external trade contractors accountable to quality standards. 📢 Apply Today! To apply, go to https://www.canisius.edu/about-canisius/employment-canisius. The review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please include your cover letter, resume and three references with their contact information, with your application. The Office of Human Resources at Canisius University utilizes an online recruitment management system. Individuals who need reasonable accommodation under the ADA in order to participate in the search process should contact the office of human resources at (716) 888-2240. Important Information: 🚨 Canisius University participates in E-Verify to confirm employment authorization. The E-Verify process is completed alongside the Form I-9 on or before your first day of work. For more details, visit www.uscis.gov ] and search \"E-Verify.\" Posted Range USD $25.65 - USD $25.65 /Hr. Options Apply Apply Submit a Referral Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://canisiusuniversity-puzzlehr.icims.com/jobs/12315/executive-associate-for-academic-affairs/job": {
      "title": "Executive Associate for Academic Affairs",
      "description": "Executive Associate for Academic Affairs Location : Location US-NY-Buffalo Category Education Position Type Full-Time Position Overview Now Hiring! Executive Associate 📍 Location: Academic Affairs 🕒 Schedule: M-F, 8:30am-5:00pm 💰 Pay: $23.08-24.10 per hour 📄 Position Type: Full-Time Why Join Canisius University Canisius University serves approximately 2,500 undergraduate and graduate students. As a Catholic and Jesuit University, Canisius has its foundation in the fundamental values of academic excellence, leadership, faith and social justice. Canisius is committed to educating and preparing men and women to become leaders in their professions and their communities, and in service to humanity. The University is an equal opportunity employer committed to recruiting, supporting, and fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff, and students. What We Offer: ✅ Salary: $23.08-24.10 per hour* ✅ Comprehensive Insurance Benefits – Health, Dental, Vision, Life and Long-Term Disability available the first of the month after the employee’s date of hire ✅ 403(b) with Company Contribution – Plan for your future with confidence – contribution from the university is available after one year of employment ✅ Paid Time Off – Includes vacation time, personal time, sick time, and paid holidays ✅ Tuition Benefits – Available for full-time employees and their qualified dependents *Please note that the compensation information is a good faith estimate of the base pay for this position. The selected candidate’s compensation package for this position will be provided during the interview process. Your Role as Executive Associate for Academic Affairs: Manage the day-to-day operations of the O ffice of Academic Affairs, including providing organizational and communications support to the Vice President, Associate Vice President, and Assistant Vice Pres ident for Academic Affairs. The Executive Associate serves as the primary point of contact for both internal and external constituencies, assisting and representing the Vice President and Associate Vice President by addressing multiple incoming issues and concerns as they arise. Manage special projects for the vice president as they are assigned. This is a full-time position with a regular work schedule from Monday through Friday, 8:30 am through 5:00 pm , except for selected instances and events as determined by the workload. Key Responsibilities: Act as the primary point of contact for both internal and external constituencies for the Office of Academic Affairs Manage schedule and day-to-day operations and administrative support for VPAA and AVPAAs as needed. Monitor scheduling activity for Board of Trustees Academics Committee, Senior Leadership Team, Committee on Faculty Status and Faculty Senate meetings. Coordinate regular communications to key Academic Affairs stakeholders. Oversee necessary social media accounts and Academic Affairs websites and ensure accuracy. Supervise support staff and student employees. Process employee transactions including but not exclusive to annual Academic Affairs appointment letters, stipend payments worksheet, payroll requests. Procard transactions, direct pay requests, honorarium payments, employee travel arrangements and expense reimbursements, new vendor set up and assist with procurement of goods and services for VPAA, Academic Affairs Endowments, Diversity & Inclusion, and COLI. Prepare annual budget analysis for Academic Affairs Division – provide justification for variance. Provide administrative support for C-STEP Program. Manage special projects for the VP as assigned. Research and compile information as needed. Prepare draft reports/presentations as needed. Assist with the VP’s correspondence. Ignatian Scholarship Day, Academic Awards Ceremony, Commencement, Honors Convocation, Academic Affairs and divisional meetings, etc. Coordinate volunteer training and assignments . Ad hoc support to Events Management , including: budgets, seating assignments/labels, certificate preparation, invitation letters, coordinating RSVP’s, etc. Provide Committee support for Faculty Senate, Committee on Faculty Status, Board of Trustees Academic Affairs Committee, CEEP Selection Committee. Maintain Faculty Evaluative Files and Chairs/Director designation in Banner. Faculty Senate Maintain roster , working with the Faculty Senate. Assist with scheduling meetings, prepare minutes, retain files, prepare agendas, and send out communications. Assist with the d evelop ment of meeting agendas and committee assignments. Track committee work and coordinate reporting. Board of Trustees – Academic Affairs Committee Schedule a meeting room and refreshments. Coordinate meeting technology and presentation needs. Prepare meeting agenda, summary , and minutes. Retain files. Send out communications. Provide administrative support for Academic Divisions, as needed. What You Need to Succeed: ✔ Qualifications: Education and Certifications A Bachelor’s degree is preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Requires strict observance of confidentiality, strong decision-making ability, close attention to detail, and accuracy and follow through. Professional demeanor required to effectively communicate with both internal and external constituencies including, University President and Vice Presidents, University Deans, students, parents, the business community, and the general public. The insight to anticipate the needs of the dean and act upon those needs without direction. The ability to graciously channel requests and calls appropriately, leaving the caller with the sense that Canisius University is concerned with their needs and wants to meet them. The ability to anticipate schedules and deadlines and move projects forward. A demonstrated history of excellent judgment, self-direction and strong interpersonal skills. Expert level verbal and written communication skills. Excellent calendar management skills, including the coordination of complex meetings. Proficient in Banner, Microsoft Office, especially Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple and diverse projects while meeting daily deadlines The ability to work evenings and weekends. Must be eligible to work in the United States. Experience Minimum 3 to 5 years demonstrated administrative support experience. 📢 Apply Today! To apply, go to https://www.canisius.edu/about-canisius/employment-canisius. The review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please include your cover letter, resume and three references with their contact information, with your application. The Office of Human Resources at Canisius University utilizes an online recruitment management system. Individuals who need reasonable accommodation under the ADA in order to participate in the search process should contact the office of human resources at (716) 888-2240. Important Information: 🚨 Canisius University participates in E-Verify to confirm employment authorization. The E-Verify process is completed alongside the Form I-9 on or before your first day of work. For more details, visit www.uscis.gov ] and search \"E-Verify.\" Posted Range USD $23.08 - USD $24.10 /Hr. Options Apply Apply Submit a Referral Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://canisiusuniversity-puzzlehr.icims.com/jobs/12165/human-resources-coordinator/job": {
      "title": "Human Resources Coordinator",
      "description": "Human Resources Coordinator Location : Location US-NY-Buffalo Category Human Resources (HR) Position Type Full-Time Position Overview Now Hiring! Human Resources Coordinator 📍 Location: Department of Human Resources 🕒 Schedule: M-F, 8:30am-4:30pm (37.5 hours per week) 💰 Pay: $20.51-$23.08 per hour 📄 Position Type: Full-Time Why Join Canisius University Canisius University serves approximately 2,500 undergraduate and graduate students. As a Catholic and Jesuit University, Canisius has its foundation in the fundamental values of academic excellence, leadership, faith and social justice. Canisius is committed to educating and preparing men and women to become leaders in their professions and their communities, and in service to humanity. The University is an equal opportunity employer committed to recruiting, supporting, and fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff, and students. What We Offer: ✅ Salary: $20.51-$23.08 per hour * ✅ Comprehensive Insurance Benefits – Health, Dental, Vision, Life and Long-Term Disability available the first of the month after the employee’s date of hire ✅ 403(b) with Company Contribution – Plan for your future with confidence – contribution from the university is available after one year of employment ✅ Paid Time Off – Includes vacation time, personal time, sick time, and paid holidays ✅ Tuition Benefits – Available for full-time employees and their qualified dependents *Please note that the compensation information is a good faith estimate of the base pay for this position. The selected candidate’s compensation package for this position will be provided during the interview process. Your Role as Human Resources Coordinator: The Human Resources Coordinator provides administrative and operational support for the Human Resources department by coordinating HR transactions, recruitment and onboarding, employee benefits, payroll support, faculty contract administration, and employee records. This position ensures compliance with employment laws and university policies, serves as a resource for faculty and staff regarding HR programs, and supports the Director of Human Resources while maintaining accurate records, overseeing office operations, and delivering exceptional customer service. Key Responsibilities: Maintain employee records, ensuring completion and accuracy of details such as Faculty contract information, pay rates, organizational structure, status changes and other key details. Maintain database for LENS program completing data entry, collection of drivers licenses and make timely notification to supervisors if necessary. Work with Deans’ staff to issue adjunct contracts each semester. Manage faculty and staff tuition waivers. Provide life insurance conversion forms and collection of laptops, keys and id cards from exiting faculty and staff. Provide customer service to faculty and staff regarding payroll, paid time off and benefits. Assist with employee engagement events. Provide administrative support to Director of Human Resources. Maintain accurate employee files and manage audit processes for compliance. Assist with coordination of all benefits, open enrollment, workers compensation, disability and paid family leave. Assist with filing Workers Compensation claims and completing paperwork requested from the insurance company. Oversee office responsibilities. Process CentreSuite and direct pay requests through BANNER and ordering of supplies. Hire, train, supervise and schedule student employees. Assist with new hire orientation and on boarding process for new faculty and staff. Assist with collection of new hire paperwork such as I-9 form and documentation, tax forms, signed offers and job descriptions, and background checks. Handle processing of I-9s through E-verify system. Run reports and process disability and paid family leave invoices. Submit University HR communication to the Dome. Handle scheduling rooms for meetings and coordinating visitor parking. Maintain general HR email inbox and respond to requests and questions. Review, track, and document compliance with mandatory and non-mandatory training which may include annual harassment training. What You Need to Succeed: ✔ Qualifications: Education & CERTIFICATIONS : A Bachelor’s degree in Human Resource Management or related field is required. Experience: Minimum of 1 year of Human Resources or related internship experience(s) is required. HRIS experience preferred. KNOWLEDGE, Skills & Abilities: Ability to work independently. A demonstrated history of excellent judgment, self-direction and strong interpersonal skills. Strong decision-making ability, strict observance of confidentiality, close attention to detail, accuracy and follow-through. The ability to anticipate schedules and deadlines and move projects forward. Expert level verbal and written communication skills. Strong analytic skills and business acumen. Proficient in Microsoft Office, especially Word, Excel and PowerPoint with the ability to learn new programs. Excellent calendar management skills, including the coordination of complex meetings. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple and diverse projects while meeting daily deadlines. Knowledge of Jesuit higher education and the University’s mission. Knowledge of Banner and Navigator systems a plus. 📢 Apply Today! To apply, go to https://www.canisius.edu/about-canisius/employment-canisius. The review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please include your cover letter, resume and three references with their contact information, with your application. The Office of Human Resources at Canisius University utilizes an online recruitment management system. Individuals who need reasonable accommodation under the ADA in order to participate in the search process should contact the office of human resources at (716) 888-2240. Important Information: 🚨 Canisius University participates in E-Verify to confirm employment authorization. The E-Verify process is completed alongside the Form I-9 on or before your first day of work. For more details, visit www.uscis.gov ] and search \"E-Verify.\" Posted Range USD $20.51 - USD $23.08 /Yr. Options Apply Apply Submit a Referral Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
